      <div class="buds-optimized-comfort__howto"> 
       <div class="buds-optimized-comfort__howto-wrap"> 
        <a href="javascript:void(0);" class="common-cta-howto js-layer-opener js-howto-popup-opener" aria-label="How to easily connect and use. Open video popup" data-target-layer="#layer-popup-how-to" data-youtube-id="T5n8o6A0Lp0" data-youtube-title="How to easily connect and use" data-howto-slide="how-to-use-easily-connect"> 
         <svg class="common-icon" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true"> 
          <use xlink:href="#wearable-play-button" href="#wearable-play-button"></use> 
         </svg> <span data-copy-set="C08-04">How to easily connect and use</span> <span class="blind" aria-hidden="true" data-copy-set="C08-06">Galaxy Buds4 Pro next to a Galaxy smartphone, explaining how to easily pair and use the two devices. Galaxy Bud4 Pro Charging Case opens and a pop-up appears on the screen of the Galaxy smartphone. "Connect" is tapped to pair the devices. On-screen tips and guides appear, explaining touch controls and head gestures. The next section introduces available settings on Galaxy Buds4 Pro. A Galaxy smartphone appears, swiping down to show the Quick Panel and the Settings icon, then tapping "Christina’s Buds4 Pro" to access noise control settings, earbud controls and customizable sound settings. The last section explains how to adjust settings from the Quick Panel. On the screen of the Galaxy smartphone is the media player. To adjust the volume, sound modes and sound settings per app, swipe down to open the Quick Panel. In the final scene, a Galaxy smartphone between a pair of Galaxy Buds4 Pro spins around as circular ripples appear in the background, representing sound waves. The video ends with the Galaxy smartphone tilted on its side, showing the rear cameras, and Galaxy Buds4 Pro floating slightly above the smartphone, with the left earbud slightly higher than the right.</span> </a> 
        <a href="javascript:void(0);" class="common-cta-howto js-layer-opener js-howto-popup-opener" aria-label="How to control effortlessly. Open video popup" data-target-layer="#layer-popup-how-to" data-youtube-id="fTYAZEYorns" data-youtube-title="How to control effortlessly" data-howto-slide="how-to-use-effortlessly"> 
         <svg class="common-icon" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true"> 
          <use xlink:href="#wearable-play-button" href="#wearable-play-button"></use> 
         </svg> <span data-copy-set="C08-10">How to control effortlessly</span> <span class="blind" aria-hidden="true" data-copy-set="C08-12">Galaxy Buds4 Pro next to a Galaxy smartphone, explaining how to easily pair and control Galaxy Buds4 Pro. Galaxy Bud4 Pro Charging Case opens and a pop-up appears on the screen of the Galaxy smartphone. "Connect" is tapped to pair the devices. The first section introduces how to use Pinch Control with a single Galaxy Buds4 Pro earbud placed in an ear canal. Demonstration of Pinch Control with a single earbud in one ear: single, double, and triple pinch to play/pause, skip forward, and go back; swipe along the earbud to adjust volume; pinch to answer calls and pinch-and-hold to decline. The next section explains how to customize controls on Galaxy Buds4 Pro. A Galaxy smartphone appears, swiping down to show the Quick Panel and the Settings icon, then tapping "Christina’s Buds4 Pro" and "Earbud controls". The second section introduces the new head gestures feature and explains how to set it up. A Galaxy smartphone appears, swiping down to show the Quick Panel and the Settings icon, then tapping "Christina’s Buds4 Pro" and toggling on "Head gestures". The next scene shows a person wearing a single Galaxy Buds4 Pro earbud while nodding to answer and shaking their head to decline a call. The last section explains how to customize voice commands from the settings menu. On the screen of the Galaxy smartphone is the settings menu. Then tap "Christina's Buds4 Pro, "Voice controls" and toggle on "Voice commands" to control Galaxy Buds4 Pro with your voice. In the final scene, a Galaxy smartphone between a pair of Galaxy Buds4 Pro spins around as circular ripples appear in the background, representing sound waves. The video ends with the Galaxy smartphone tilted on its side, showing the rear cameras, and Galaxy Buds4 Pro floating slightly above the smartphone, with the left earbud slightly higher than the right.</span> </a> 
       </div> 
      </div> 
