        <li class="common-bottom-disclaimer__list-item" role="listitem" data-sup="sup-3"> <span class="text_disclaimer" data-copy-set="disclaimer">Wireless charger and cable sold separately.</span> <button type="button" class="common-bottom-disclaimer__back-cta"> <span class="sr-only">Back to Location</span> 
          <svg class="common-icon" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true"> 
           <use xlink:href="#wearable-disclaimer-top" href="#wearable-disclaimer-top"></use> 
          </svg> </button> </li> 
        <li class="common-bottom-disclaimer__list-item" role="listitem" data-sup="sup-4"> <span class="text_disclaimer" data-copy-set="disclaimer">Based on global ear data research conducted by Samsung Design Innovation Center.</span> <button type="button" class="common-bottom-disclaimer__back-cta"> <span class="sr-only">Back to Location</span> 
          <svg class="common-icon" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true"> 
           <use xlink:href="#wearable-disclaimer-top" href="#wearable-disclaimer-top"></use> 
          </svg> </button> </li> 
        <li class="common-bottom-disclaimer__list-item" role="listitem" data-sup="sup-5"> <span class="text_disclaimer" data-copy-set="disclaimer">The new wider woofer on Galaxy Buds4 Pro has 19.8% larger diaphragm compared to Galaxy Buds3 Pro.</span> <button type="button" class="common-bottom-disclaimer__back-cta"> <span class="sr-only">Back to Location</span> 
          <svg class="common-icon" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true"> 
           <use xlink:href="#wearable-disclaimer-top" href="#wearable-disclaimer-top"></use> 
          </svg> </button> </li> 
        <li class="common-bottom-disclaimer__list-item" role="listitem" data-sup="sup-6"> <span class="text_disclaimer" data-copy-set="disclaimer">Ultra High Quality Audio (UHQ) up to 24-bit / 96 kHz is available on Galaxy S26 Series, S25 Series, S24 Series, S23 Series, Z Fold7, Z Flip7, Z Fold6, Z Flip6, Z Fold5, Z Flip5 and Tab S11 Series, Tab S10 Series, Tab S9 Series with One UI 6.1.1 or above. Additional devices may be supported in the future.</span> <button type="button" class="common-bottom-disclaimer__back-cta"> <span class="sr-only">Back to Location</span> 
          <svg class="common-icon" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true"> 
           <use xlink:href="#wearable-disclaimer-top" href="#wearable-disclaimer-top"></use> 
          </svg> </button> </li> 
        <li class="common-bottom-disclaimer__list-item" role="listitem" data-sup="sup-7"> <span class="text_disclaimer" data-copy-set="disclaimer">UHQ is off by default and can be configured directly in the phone settings for devices running One UI 8.0 and later. For devices running on earlier versions of One UI, configurations can be found in the Galaxy Wearable app.</span> <button type="button" class="common-bottom-disclaimer__back-cta"> <span class="sr-only">Back to Location</span> 
          <svg class="common-icon" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true"> 
           <use xlink:href="#wearable-disclaimer-top" href="#wearable-disclaimer-top"></use> 
          </svg> </button> </li> 
        <li class="common-bottom-disclaimer__list-item" role="listitem" data-sup="sup-8"> <span class="text_disclaimer" data-copy-set="disclaimer">360 Audio is only available on Samsung Galaxy smartphones and Galaxy Tab devices with Android One UI version 3.1 or later, and selected Samsung TV models. Supported Samsung TV models include: Neo QLED 8K (QN900D, QN800D), Neo QLED 4K (QN95D, QN90D, QN87D, QN85D) OLED (S95D, S90D, S85D), QLED (Q80D, Q70D). Support for 360 Audio and head tracking may vary depending on the application and content.</span> <button type="button" class="common-bottom-disclaimer__back-cta"> <span class="sr-only">Back to Location</span> 
          <svg class="common-icon" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true"> 
           <use xlink:href="#wearable-disclaimer-top" href="#wearable-disclaimer-top"></use> 
          </svg> </button> </li> 
        <li class="common-bottom-disclaimer__list-item" role="listitem" data-sup="sup-9"> <span class="text_disclaimer" data-copy-set="disclaimer">Super wideband (SWB) call is available on Galaxy S26 series, S25 series, Z Fold7, Z Flip7, Z Fold6, Z Flip6, A56, Tab S11 series and Tab S10 series with One UI 6.1.1 or above. Additional devices may be supported in the future. Super wideband call is available regardless of the call app. SWB may not be supported depending on the mobile network between devices.</span> <button type="button" class="common-bottom-disclaimer__back-cta"> <span class="sr-only">Back to Location</span> 
          <svg class="common-icon" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true"> 
           <use xlink:href="#wearable-disclaimer-top" href="#wearable-disclaimer-top"></use> 
          </svg> </button> </li> 
        <li class="common-bottom-disclaimer__list-item" role="listitem" data-sup="sup-10"> <span class="text_disclaimer" data-copy-set="disclaimer">Each earbud contains three microphones (six in total across the device). The advanced DNN technology processes audio independently on each earbud, with no interaction between them.</span> <button type="button" class="common-bottom-disclaimer__back-cta"> <span class="sr-only">Back to Location</span> 
          <svg class="common-icon" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true"> 
           <use xlink:href="#wearable-disclaimer-top" href="#wearable-disclaimer-top"></use> 
          </svg> </button> </li> 
        <li class="common-bottom-disclaimer__list-item" role="listitem" data-sup="sup-11"> <span class="text_disclaimer" data-copy-set="disclaimer">Adaptive Noise Control, Voice Detect and Siren Detect are off by default, and can be configured directly in the phone settings for devices running One UI 8.0 and later. For devices running on earlier versions of One UI, configurations can be found in the Galaxy Wearable app.</span> <button type="button" class="common-bottom-disclaimer__back-cta"> <span class="sr-only">Back to Location</span> 
          <svg class="common-icon" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true"> 
           <use xlink:href="#wearable-disclaimer-top" href="#wearable-disclaimer-top"></use> 
          </svg> </button> </li> 
        <li class="common-bottom-disclaimer__list-item" role="listitem" data-sup="sup-12"> <span class="text_disclaimer" data-copy-set="disclaimer">Bluetooth must be turned on to pair Galaxy Buds4 Pro with Galaxy smartphone and Galaxy Tab.</span> <button type="button" class="common-bottom-disclaimer__back-cta"> <span class="sr-only">Back to Location</span> 
          <svg class="common-icon" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true"> 
           <use xlink:href="#wearable-disclaimer-top" href="#wearable-disclaimer-top"></use> 
          </svg> </button> </li> 
        <li class="common-bottom-disclaimer__list-item" role="listitem" data-sup="sup-13"> <span class="text_disclaimer" data-copy-set="disclaimer">Additional plug-in may need to be downloaded based on the version of One UI. For devices running on One UI versions below 8.0, Galaxy Wearable app needs to be downloaded.</span> <button type="button" class="common-bottom-disclaimer__back-cta"> <span class="sr-only">Back to Location</span> 
          <svg class="common-icon" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true"> 
           <use xlink:href="#wearable-disclaimer-top" href="#wearable-disclaimer-top"></use> 
          </svg> </button> </li> 
        <li class="common-bottom-disclaimer__list-item" role="listitem" data-sup="sup-14"> <span class="text_disclaimer" data-copy-set="disclaimer">Connecting Samsung Galaxy Buds4 Pro as Bluetooth Audio is available regardless of OS but to configure advanced settings on the Galaxy Wearable app, Samsung Galaxy Buds4 Pro must be paired with a smartphone with Android 12.0 or above and minimum 1.5 GB Memory.</span> <button type="button" class="common-bottom-disclaimer__back-cta"> <span class="sr-only">Back to Location</span> 
          <svg class="common-icon" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true"> 
           <use xlink:href="#wearable-disclaimer-top" href="#wearable-disclaimer-top"></use> 
          </svg> </button> </li> 
        <li class="common-bottom-disclaimer__list-item" role="listitem" data-sup="sup-15"> <span class="text_disclaimer" data-copy-set="disclaimer">Samsung Account login is required to activate and change Galaxy Buds4 Pro settings on the Galaxy Wearable app.</span> <button type="button" class="common-bottom-disclaimer__back-cta"> <span class="sr-only">Back to Location</span> 
          <svg class="common-icon" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true"> 
           <use xlink:href="#wearable-disclaimer-top" href="#wearable-disclaimer-top"></use> 
          </svg> </button> </li> 
        <li class="common-bottom-disclaimer__list-item" role="listitem" data-sup="sup-16"> <span class="text_disclaimer" data-copy-set="disclaimer">Samsung Account login is required to activate and change Galaxy Buds4 Pro settings. For devices running on One UI 8.0 or later, settings can be configured directly in the phone settings. For devices running on earlier versions, configurations can be found in the Galaxy Wearable app. Additionally, to use the Galaxy Wearable app, Samsung Galaxy Buds4 Pro must be paired with a smartphone running Android 12.0 or above with at least 1.5 GB of memory. Galaxy Wearable app is not supported on iOS.</span> <button type="button" class="common-bottom-disclaimer__back-cta"> <span class="sr-only">Back to Location</span> 
          <svg class="common-icon" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true"> 
           <use xlink:href="#wearable-disclaimer-top" href="#wearable-disclaimer-top"></use> 
          </svg> </button> </li> 
        <li class="common-bottom-disclaimer__list-item" role="listitem" data-sup="sup-17"> <span class="text_disclaimer" data-copy-set="disclaimer">Connecting Samsung Galaxy Buds4 Pro as Bluetooth Audio is available regardless of the OS.</span> <button type="button" class="common-bottom-disclaimer__back-cta"> <span class="sr-only">Back to Location</span> 
          <svg class="common-icon" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true"> 
           <use xlink:href="#wearable-disclaimer-top" href="#wearable-disclaimer-top"></use> 
          </svg> </button> </li> 
        <li class="common-bottom-disclaimer__list-item" role="listitem" data-sup="sup-18"> <span class="text_disclaimer" data-copy-set="disclaimer">Interpreter is available on smartphone devices with Galaxy AI features included, running on One UI 6.1.1 or later.</span> <button type="button" class="common-bottom-disclaimer__back-cta"> <span class="sr-only">Back to Location</span> 
          <svg class="common-icon" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true"> 
           <use xlink:href="#wearable-disclaimer-top" href="#wearable-disclaimer-top"></use> 
          </svg> </button> </li> 
        <li class="common-bottom-disclaimer__list-item" role="listitem" data-sup="sup-19"> <span class="text_disclaimer" data-copy-set="disclaimer">Galaxy Buds4 Pro supports Galaxy AI features such as Interpreter and Live Translate when paired with compatible Samsung Galaxy devices. Availability of Galaxy AI features may vary by device model. Samsung Account login may be required to use certain Samsung AI features. Samsung does not make any promises, assurances or guarantees as to the accuracy, completeness or reliability of the output provided by AI features. Supported languages (Regions) are Arabic, Bahasa Indonesia, Chinese Simplified, Chinese Traditional (Hong Kong, Taiwan), Dutch, English (Australia, India, United Kingdom, United States), French (Canada, France), German, Hindi, Italian, Japanese, Korean, Polish, Portuguese (Brazil, Portugal), Romanian, Russian (Russian Federation), Spanish (Mexico, Spain, United States), Swedish, Thai, Turkish, Vietnamese, Tagalog, Gujarati. More languages will be added in future updates.</span> <button type="button" class="common-bottom-disclaimer__back-cta"> <span class="sr-only">Back to Location</span> 
          <svg class="common-icon" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true"> 
           <use xlink:href="#wearable-disclaimer-top" href="#wearable-disclaimer-top"></use> 
          </svg> </button> </li> 
        <li class="common-bottom-disclaimer__list-item" role="listitem" data-sup="sup-20"> <span class="text_disclaimer" data-copy-set="disclaimer">Voice wake-up is off by default, and can be configured directly in the phone settings for devices running One UI 8.0 and later. For devices running on earlier versions of One UI, configurations can be found in the Galaxy Wearable app.</span> <button type="button" class="common-bottom-disclaimer__back-cta"> <span class="sr-only">Back to Location</span> 
          <svg class="common-icon" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true"> 
           <use xlink:href="#wearable-disclaimer-top" href="#wearable-disclaimer-top"></use> 
          </svg> </button> </li> 
        <li class="common-bottom-disclaimer__list-item" role="listitem" data-sup="sup-21"> <span class="text_disclaimer" data-copy-set="disclaimer">Bixby is supported on most Samsung Galaxy smartphones and Galaxy Tab devices. Bixby provides real-time answers on devices running on One UI 8.5 or later. Service availability may vary by country, service provider, device model and OS version.</span> <button type="button" class="common-bottom-disclaimer__back-cta"> <span class="sr-only">Back to Location</span> 
          <svg class="common-icon" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true"> 
           <use xlink:href="#wearable-disclaimer-top" href="#wearable-disclaimer-top"></use> 
          </svg> </button> </li> 
        <li class="common-bottom-disclaimer__list-item" role="listitem" data-sup="sup-22"> <span class="text_disclaimer" data-copy-set="disclaimer">Bixby supports 9 languages: Korean, English, German, French, Italian, Spanish, Portuguese, Chinese (Simplified) and Japanese.</span> <button type="button" class="common-bottom-disclaimer__back-cta"> <span class="sr-only">Back to Location</span> 
          <svg class="common-icon" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true"> 
           <use xlink:href="#wearable-disclaimer-top" href="#wearable-disclaimer-top"></use> 
          </svg> </button> </li> 
        <li class="common-bottom-disclaimer__list-item" role="listitem" data-sup="sup-23"> <span class="text_disclaimer" data-copy-set="disclaimer">Head Gesture is off by default, and can be configured directly in the phone settings for paired devices running One UI 8.5 and later.</span> <button type="button" class="common-bottom-disclaimer__back-cta"> <span class="sr-only">Back to Location</span> 
          <svg class="common-icon" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true"> 
           <use xlink:href="#wearable-disclaimer-top" href="#wearable-disclaimer-top"></use> 
          </svg> </button> </li> 
        <li class="common-bottom-disclaimer__list-item" role="listitem" data-sup="sup-24"> <span class="text_disclaimer" data-copy-set="disclaimer">Supported apps may vary by country. Gestures can be set by the user.</span> <button type="button" class="common-bottom-disclaimer__back-cta"> <span class="sr-only">Back to Location</span> 
          <svg class="common-icon" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true"> 
           <use xlink:href="#wearable-disclaimer-top" href="#wearable-disclaimer-top"></use> 
          </svg> </button> </li> 
        <li class="common-bottom-disclaimer__list-item" role="listitem" data-sup="sup-25"> <span class="text_disclaimer" data-copy-set="disclaimer">Auto Switch feature is only available on Samsung Galaxy Book series with One UI 6.0 Book or later, Samsung Galaxy smartphones and Galaxy Tab devices with One UI 4.1.1 or later and Galaxy Watch4 series or later. Samsung Galaxy devices must be logged in to Samsung Account to enable the Auto Switch feature. Auto Switch feature for Samsung TV is only available on Samsung TVs launched Feb ’22 or later after getting a firmware update from Jul ’22. Auto Switch with TV is only available for making and receiving phone calls.</span> <button type="button" class="common-bottom-disclaimer__back-cta"> <span class="sr-only">Back to Location</span> 
          <svg class="common-icon" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true"> 
           <use xlink:href="#wearable-disclaimer-top" href="#wearable-disclaimer-top"></use> 
          </svg> </button> </li> 
        <li class="common-bottom-disclaimer__list-item" role="listitem" data-sup="sup-26"> <span class="text_disclaimer" data-copy-set="disclaimer">Galaxy Buds4 Pro can be connected to iOS devices but cannot be controlled through the device as Galaxy Wearable app is not supported.</span> <button type="button" class="common-bottom-disclaimer__back-cta"> <span class="sr-only">Back to Location</span> 
          <svg class="common-icon" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true"> 
           <use xlink:href="#wearable-disclaimer-top" href="#wearable-disclaimer-top"></use> 
          </svg> </button> </li> 
        <li class="common-bottom-disclaimer__list-item" role="listitem" data-sup="sup-28"> <span class="text_disclaimer" data-copy-set="disclaimer">Actual battery life may vary and depend on usage conditions, settings, number of times charged, Bluetooth signal strength, and other factors.</span> <button type="button" class="common-bottom-disclaimer__back-cta"> <span class="sr-only">Back to Location</span> 
          <svg class="common-icon" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true"> 
           <use xlink:href="#wearable-disclaimer-top" href="#wearable-disclaimer-top"></use> 
          </svg> </button> </li> 
        <li class="common-bottom-disclaimer__list-item" role="listitem" data-sup="sup-29"> <span class="text_disclaimer" data-copy-set="disclaimer">Actual Play time may vary based on settings.</span> <button type="button" class="common-bottom-disclaimer__back-cta"> <span class="sr-only">Back to Location</span> 
          <svg class="common-icon" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true"> 
           <use xlink:href="#wearable-disclaimer-top" href="#wearable-disclaimer-top"></use> 
          </svg> </button> </li> 
        <li class="common-bottom-disclaimer__list-item" role="listitem" data-sup="sup-30"> <span class="text_disclaimer" data-copy-set="disclaimer">Galaxy Buds use LC3 Codec when audio is transmitted over LE Audio. The availability of LE Audio may vary depending on the paired device and the audio features used. For LE Audio to function, the paired device must support it.</span> <button type="button" class="common-bottom-disclaimer__back-cta"> <span class="sr-only">Back to Location</span> 
          <svg class="common-icon" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true"> 
           <use xlink:href="#wearable-disclaimer-top" href="#wearable-disclaimer-top"></use> 
          </svg> </button> </li> 
        <li class="common-bottom-disclaimer__list-item" role="listitem" data-sup="sup-31"> <span class="text_disclaimer" data-copy-set="disclaimer">Auracast™ is a trademark of Bluetooth SIG, Inc.</span> <button type="button" class="common-bottom-disclaimer__back-cta"> <span class="sr-only">Back to Location</span> 
          <svg class="common-icon" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true"> 
           <use xlink:href="#wearable-disclaimer-top" href="#wearable-disclaimer-top"></use> 
          </svg> </button> </li> 
        <li class="common-bottom-disclaimer__list-item" role="listitem" data-sup="sup-32"> <span class="text_disclaimer" data-copy-set="disclaimer">IP57 is based on laboratory test conditions for submersion in up to 1 meter of fresh water for up to 30 minutes.</span> <button type="button" class="common-bottom-disclaimer__back-cta"> <span class="sr-only">Back to Location</span> 
          <svg class="common-icon" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true"> 
           <use xlink:href="#wearable-disclaimer-top" href="#wearable-disclaimer-top"></use> 
          </svg> </button> </li> 
        <li class="common-bottom-disclaimer__list-item" role="listitem" data-sup="sup-33"> <span class="text_disclaimer" data-copy-set="disclaimer">Not advised for beach or pool use. Charging Case is not water resistant. If the earbuds are damaged, they are not guaranteed to be water resistant. If the earbuds or your hands are wet, they must be dried thoroughly prior to handling or placing into the Charging Case. If placed into the Charging Case without drying, the earbuds may be damaged.</span> <button type="button" class="common-bottom-disclaimer__back-cta"> <span class="sr-only">Back to Location</span> 
          <svg class="common-icon" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true"> 
           <use xlink:href="#wearable-disclaimer-top" href="#wearable-disclaimer-top"></use> 
          </svg> </button> </li> 
       </ol> 
      </div> 
     </div> 
    </div> 
   </div> 
  </div> 
